<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Randgold forecasts profit, changes yr-end.</title>
<headline>Randgold forecasts profit, changes yr-end.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Forecast for year ended September 30, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)		 63	    vs 61</p>
<p>    Post excep shr (cents) 126	  vs  316</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 nil	   vs  10</p>
<p>    Net profit		48.69	 vs 119.71</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   70.50	 vs 119.90</p>
<p>    Tax			 19.07	 vs 0.18</p>
<p>    Net tax		   51.43	 vs 119.71</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   nil	   vs 0.325</p>
<p>    Interest received     20.33	 vs 9.09</p>
<p>    Turnover		  60.11	 vs 75.51</p>
<p>Full name: Randgold &amp; Exploration Co Ltd</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     27.60 gain  vs 96.711 gain</p>
<p>NOTE - Gold mining firm Randgold said it was making a profit forecast for the year to end September because the firm is changing its year-end date to March 31.</p>
<p>The next set of Randgold results will cover the eighteen months from October 1, 1995 to March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
